WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.820
- Our next guest is a Grammy-winning

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:03.780
musician with her band Sugarland.

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:05.750
She's out now with a Broadway-themed album

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:06.900
that drops this Friday,

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.610
it's called Always Like New.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.409
Say hello to my girl, Jennifer Nettles.

00:00:11.409 --> 00:00:15.492
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:23.953
I know, we can do,

00:00:23.953 --> 00:00:24.786
maybe that.

00:00:24.786 --> 00:00:26.680
We might not get fired for that.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.374
I love your outfit!

00:00:28.374 --> 00:00:29.461
- Thank you, likewise.

00:00:29.461 --> 00:00:30.294
Meow.

00:00:30.294 --> 00:00:31.127
- Oh thank you, oh my gosh,

00:00:31.127 --> 00:00:32.920
yeah well you get it, but

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.320
it's like some days, you're like okay...

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.215
- You're killing it.

00:00:36.215 --> 00:00:37.048
She's killing it, isn't she?

00:00:37.048 --> 00:00:38.930
- No, I love your outfit, I
haven't seen you in forever.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:39.763
- It's been a minute.

00:00:39.763 --> 00:00:41.183
- Yeah well I haven't
seen anyone in forever.

00:00:41.183 --> 00:00:42.414
- It's been a hot minute for everybody

00:00:42.414 --> 00:00:43.247
'cause also we've been in like

00:00:43.247 --> 00:00:44.140
a year that disappeared.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.210
- Yes. It's gone.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.043
- So, yeah gone.

00:00:46.043 --> 00:00:46.980
- It's gone, it's fine.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.300
But how has your family been?

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.610
- Everybody is good,

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.360
everybody is good considering.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.193
- Yeah.

00:00:52.193 --> 00:00:53.026
- You know, I mean,

00:00:53.026 --> 00:00:54.870
I think the kids are way
more resilient than we are

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:55.703
at this point.

00:00:55.703 --> 00:00:56.536
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:56.536 --> 00:00:57.650
- I feel like all of our resilience

00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:58.582
this year has just been like

00:00:58.582 --> 00:00:59.415
(imitates airplane crashing)

00:00:59.415 --> 00:01:00.248
gone, you know?

00:01:00.248 --> 00:01:01.270
- I think as soon as Disneyland opened up,

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:02.244
my kids were fine.

00:01:02.244 --> 00:01:03.590
(laughing)

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:05.440
They were like it's
fine, Disneyland's back,

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.894
everything is going to be fine.

00:01:06.894 --> 00:01:08.344
- Good. The world is right.

00:01:08.344 --> 00:01:09.960
- The world is now spinning again.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.770
But I heard that you performed
at your son's school.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:14.700
Was he, is he at the age
where he thinks it's cool?

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.450
Or is he kind of like, "Oh mom."?

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:17.283
- He was so,

00:01:17.283 --> 00:01:18.270
you know it's interesting,

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:19.610
sometimes he can take it or leave it.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.072
He was super proud that day.

00:01:21.072 --> 00:01:21.905
- [Kelly] Aw!

00:01:21.905 --> 00:01:22.738
- Of course this wasn't this year,

00:01:22.738 --> 00:01:23.571
'cause as I said, he wasn't there.

00:01:23.571 --> 00:01:24.571
Oh yeah, there's the picture,

00:01:24.571 --> 00:01:25.600
precious art.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:26.779
Oh my God, I want to eat him.

00:01:26.779 --> 00:01:27.612
- [Kelly] Look at that awesome picture.

00:01:27.612 --> 00:01:29.730
- Yeah so he loved it then though,

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:30.910
he was super proud then

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:34.290
and some days he's like
"yeah, no please, just go on.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:35.600
Do not sing, move along."

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:36.650
- That's all of our kids.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.280
Some days they're so
proud, and then other days

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.490
they tell people Nick Jonas
is their favorite Voice Coach

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:41.460
and you're like, "Sure."

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.450
- You're like, "Fine."

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:45.770
- Sure, yeah Jumanji was cool, I guess.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:46.603
- Yes.

00:01:46.603 --> 00:01:48.040
- So how old were you when
you started performing?

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:48.873
I don't think we ever
even talked about that

00:01:48.873 --> 00:01:50.320
when we worked on duets years ago.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:51.720
- I know, all those years ago.
- Yeah.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:54.201
- You know what, I started in
church, like most of us do,

00:01:54.201 --> 00:01:55.034
- Oh okay, yeah.

00:01:55.034 --> 00:01:56.120
when I was about six years old.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:57.720
- Oh wow, that young?
- [Jennifer] Yeah.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:58.660
- Wow.
- [Jennifer] Yeah.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:01:59.493
- That's awesome.

00:01:59.493 --> 00:02:00.326
- [Jennifer] Children's choir,

00:02:00.326 --> 00:02:02.080
- Yes! Represent! I did that as well.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.140
- Doing the Christmas pageant that we did,

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.800
and the Children's Choir Director,

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:07.990
Ms. Kathy Vickers,

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:09.310
thank you, yes,

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:10.397
she went to my mom and said,

00:02:10.397 --> 00:02:12.560
"You know, I think Jennifer
has some propensity for

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.800
music and maybe you should
put her in piano lessons."

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.340
She was also the town piano teacher,

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.173
so that worked out real well for her.

00:02:17.173 --> 00:02:18.210
- So she's getting some work.

00:02:19.051 --> 00:02:20.830
- [Jennifer] She was drumming
up, she was hustling.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:21.965
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:02:21.965 --> 00:02:22.798
- It turned out well.

00:02:22.798 --> 00:02:23.631
- It turned out really well.

00:02:23.631 --> 00:02:25.460
Have you always loved Broadway?

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:27.319
Cause the new album is all Broadway.

00:02:27.319 --> 00:02:28.152
- Yes, always.

00:02:28.152 --> 00:02:29.070
It's all Broadway, and I've
always wanted to do this

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.150
record.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.890
For me, it has been the most,

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:33.780
and I know you've had
these kinds of records,

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.831
that feel the most vocally exciting.

00:02:35.831 --> 00:02:36.664
- Yeah.

00:02:36.664 --> 00:02:37.940
- And the most vocally expansive,

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:39.790
especially because as
artists sometimes if we get

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.150
pegged with one sound...

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:42.890
- [Kelly] 100%, that's why
I love Christmas albums.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:43.797
You can do whatever you want.

00:02:43.797 --> 00:02:44.650
- Me too! You can do
whatever you want and nobody

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:45.483
says anything.

00:02:45.483 --> 00:02:46.710
- Yeah.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:47.660
- Nobody cries, nobody
fusses, nobody whines.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.040
- Yeah, yeah, just sounds classic.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:51.170
- So I've always wanted to do
this because I grew up doing

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:52.003
theater.

00:02:52.003 --> 00:02:54.500
I grew up, you know, in community
theater, in high school,

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.420
in college, all throughout.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:57.980
And I always really
wanted to get back to it.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:00.680
Super thankful for the
success I had as a musician,

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:04.090
but also thankful that that
success has let me enter into

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:05.800
then the theater community at a place,

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.630
because you came and
saw me years ago like...

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:09.112
- [Kelly] Yes, I did.

00:03:09.112 --> 00:03:09.945
- In Chicago.

00:03:09.945 --> 00:03:10.778
- And you were fricking awesome.

00:03:10.778 --> 00:03:11.920
And I've always wanted to,

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:12.850
I'm a nerd for Broadway too.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:13.724
- [Jennifer] I know you are!

00:03:13.724 --> 00:03:14.557
- I grew up with musical theater

00:03:14.557 --> 00:03:18.060
and so I'm envious of this whole project

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.012
and I was envious and just
so elated for you as well.

00:03:21.012 --> 00:03:21.845
- Thank you.

00:03:21.845 --> 00:03:22.678
- [Kelly] You shine so bright.

00:03:22.678 --> 00:03:23.511
- You get it though.

00:03:23.511 --> 00:03:25.330
It's like, it holds a place
in your heart and it really,

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:26.300
I think informs.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.780
- It's a hard thing to do, too.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:28.613
Broadway is hard.

00:03:28.613 --> 00:03:30.100
Like it's a big schedule.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:30.933
- It's a, yes.

00:03:30.933 --> 00:03:32.470
- If you can nail that, you're amazing.

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:33.712
- It's a big schedule.

00:03:33.712 --> 00:03:34.545
- Yeah.

00:03:34.545 --> 00:03:36.580
- But it's just so
enriching and so worth it.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:38.400
And I think, you know,
the music itself just,

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.233
as you're saying,

00:03:39.233 --> 00:03:42.980
is so informative as an artist,
and I know you get this too

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:43.813
as a performer,

00:03:43.813 --> 00:03:45.400
you know, you learn about what it is to be

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:46.600
a character in a song,

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.310
you learn about what it is to embody that.

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:51.450
- It's not that far from country, to me.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.530
Like country music is all story-telling.

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:53.900
- It's all story-telling,
it's all story-telling.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:54.790
- Yeah, that's why when every,

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:55.670
- For sure.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:56.503
- They said you were doing
the album, I was like,

00:03:56.503 --> 00:03:57.720
"Well, it's like more story-telling."

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.120
- Obvious, not a big leap.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.560
- Yeah, I love it.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.530
Do you remember the very
first Broadway show that you

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:03.363
ever saw?

00:04:03.363 --> 00:04:04.511
- Yes I do, on Broadway more specifically,

00:04:04.511 --> 00:04:07.440
because I was in the third grade.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:08.470
- [Kelly] Wow, lucky.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:10.660
- Yeah, super lucky,
because my aunt and uncle,

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.330
my Aunt K and my Uncle Walter,

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:15.600
took me and my cousin,
Allison, on an Amtrak train,

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.130
from Jessup, Georgia,

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.950
all the way up to New York City.

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:20.540
So this is my Aunt Cora
Lee and Uncle Jerry,

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:21.820
my great aunt and uncle

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.350
and they lived in New York City.

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:24.990
They still do, well he passed this year.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.400
But they took us to see A Chorus Line.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.990
- Oh wow! That was your first?

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:31.760
- It was very racy for a young girl,

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.330
I was scandalized in some ways,

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.830
but absolutely mesmerized in most ways,

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:38.270
in the world that they
created on that stage.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:40.430
And she took me outside
afterwards, and she said,

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:41.907
in her best New York accent,

00:04:41.907 --> 00:04:43.250
"Jennifer, what did you think?"

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:44.197
And I said,

00:04:44.197 --> 00:04:45.710
"I'll be back."

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:46.923
- Oh my God, you were full-on Terminator.

00:04:46.923 --> 00:04:48.933
- Yes, yes, full-on Terminator.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:53.860
- And I can't wait for
Broadway to get back.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:54.750
Like, to feel that energy.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:56.530
- And it's coming back, it's coming back.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:59.560
September, there's going to be
some soft openings happening.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:01.753
- Yeah. Oh my God, I'm so excited for you.

